Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 5.3 Conditions to the Obligations of Parent and Merger Sub. The obligations of Parent and Merger Sub to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Article III shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that do not have a Material Adverse Effect, provided that the representations and warranties in Sections 3.1(a), 3.3, and 3.4 shall be true and correct in all respects without exception as of the Closing Date. (ii) All other representations and warranties set forth in this Agreement shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the Closing Date, except for any inaccuracies that do not have a Material Adverse Effect, unless such representations and warranties expressly speak as of an earlier date, in which case they must be true and correct as of such earlier date. (Pages 112-113)\nAnswer:
